A||||9||EdsB52||Why threaten?||||1||
Z||000000||EdsB52||08-12-2001||10:19 AM||||My apologies to Cliff, as he's told us not to do this, but I feel this situation warrants it. I promised not to post in that thread if, “As I said, if all parties drop this thread, I will also.” Well, since then 29 posts have been added including one from Cliff basically saying take it elsewhere. I didn’t write “Both parties,” I wrote “all parties.” That means people should have avoided that thread if they wanted to make peace. Well, it appears that some forum members aren’t sincere when they tell someone to quit posting. What they really mean is to stand there and let everyone take free shots. Me and the other party have apparently made amends and I am not directing this thread at him. I’m willing to let the hostilities go, but am also willing to be back in it if necessary. I have let some people in there have the last word multiple times over, but will ensue action if people don’t drop it. I’m not conceding, and don’t ask anyone else to, but am tired of getting trashed without response. Maybe some of the other members can bring sense to all of it. Now to be clear, I may have somewhat the same writing/arguing style in the future, but will try to be more conscious of insults I cast. If my so-called arrogant writing style pisses you off, don’t read. I have refrained, against my will, from commenting on many attacks leveled against me, but I will not let this particular one go unanswered. MACH10 wrote:<P><BR>“I was going to email Ed with this question, but I'm too lazy to open OE right now:<BR>Why do you do this? Do you truly feel that people are impressed with what you have to say? It seems that when you run out of ideas, you bash spelling or grammatical mistakes. I don't run my work through a spellchecker. I don't usually need it. I'm a 4th year Anthro major, and I screw up all the time. I guess I must be pretty stupid. Any idiot can spend 15 minutes writing a 4-line post with a thesaurus in his hand. Big vocabulary does not make one smarter than the other, neither does perfect grammar. Saying "3 + 3 = 6" in perfect english using large mathematical terms does not make you a mathematician.<P>You seem to revel in the bad attention you recieve from the vast majority of the people reading the posts. Most likely, not everyone hates you, true. Most people here don't hate you. I don't. I find you annoying and crass, and I'm sure others here feel the same.<P>Telling me that you're sleeping with my wife would not go down easy. 6'10@215 or not, expect to be discovering a whole new world of pain and physiotherapy by a wimpy 5'6, 180lb 21 year old male. You knock ME cold, fair enough, but you still have to deal with a shattered elbow. Size matters not. In any case, I'm not married, nor is my girlfriend even in the same country as you, so I put that scenario in the "not applicable" pile.<P>Now, I realize that this is adding to the fire. Ed, I suggest you respond to me, in person, via email. If you have anything intelligent to say to me, go right ahead. Just remove the spam-blocks:<BR>umfoggsd&lt;at&gt;mail&lt;dot&gt;cc&lt;dot&gt;umanitoba&lt;dot&gt;ca<P>In the mean time, I will add my vote to the increasing pile of people that believe that you are an immature little man with a couple of grammar, legal, and dictionary texts within easy reach. Why don't you try being agreable for a change? Not every post needs a tasteless comment added by you. You don't have to agree, but you don't need to be so damn obnoxious. Write back soon, dearie.”<P>First of all I posted that I’m 6’1”, 215, not 6’10”, 215. The latter would be like dikembe Mutumbo, not very scary. The context for me relating that information was this:<BR>“Dude, if your going to make comments about somebody's wife/fiancee/girlfriend, then you better not make it sound so serious. You know what would happen if you said that to somebody one on one? You'd probably get your lights knocked out.”<BR>The above was posted by a member. I then replied in part with this:<BR>“Guys in this forum love to generalize and make assumptions based on scant information. I'm 6'1", 215, and in good shape. What if I said that to an 18 year old kid who was 5'10" 150? What if I said that to a 60-year-old man? What if I said that to a guy that was 6'3", 250, but meek? Don't get me wrong, I'm not a bully, but nothing would happen in these scenarios. I wouldn't insult someone unless provoked anyway.”<BR>So I’m not 6’10”, nor am I a bully as I previously stated by MACH 10. By posting my size I was bringing some clarity to a generalization that was made. I’m not big, I’m of average size. Now that I’ve contextualized that irrelevant data, I’ll tie it together with MACH 10’s post. MACH 10 asserted that I would discover a whole new world of pain and physiotherapy if I made remarks to your wife, even though you’re not married. He further made reference to a shattered elbow. Well this is a hypothetical situation; so let me give a hypothetical answer. Let’s assume you are married and I made that comment to you. Would you leave Canada, drive or fly to Phoenix, locate me, knock on my door or stalk me, then approach me to lay some hurtin’ down? Do you want intelligent people to believe you would throw your life away to vindicate a few words over the Internet? Even I don’t know the process involved in International prosecution, in the case someone called the cops on a disturbance/disorderly conduct charge. Could you imagine the explanation someone would undergo as they relate the notion that they came from thousands of miles away from another country because someone pissed them off over the net? They could possibly prosecute you internationally, US Federally, the State of Arizona, and possibly Federally and/or Territorially in Canada. Remember, double jeopardy is when you are tried for the same crime twice in the SAME JURISDICTION. The last part is the one most commonly forgotten. Possibly 4 or 5 prosecutions run consecutively. Now would they? Probably not. The State of Arizona would be the prosecuting jurisdiction most likely. Now, back to the issue. With this information, do you want intelligent people to believe you would risk your entire life to vindicate a post on an Internet club? No, of course not. So answer me this; why cast empty threats to punctuate your hate/dislike for me when you would never satisfy them? I tolerate a bunch of crap, as well as dish it out. But what I don’t tolerate are threats. These threats are based on a hypothetical, so I’ll retort by saying you wouldn’t perform the asserted threats even if you had a wife, and you look silly casting threats that wouldn’t be fulfilled even if I replicated my deed. Would you fulfill your threats if I replicated my deed to your girlfriend? The spirit of your threats are made to intimidate and to submit your vote of disapproval, so why not just do the latter? One thing written that I agree with is that 5’6” 180 can be a tough disposition. That’s very stocky; are you fat? If not, that’s a tough build to defeat. Size has little to do with that which predicates the “winner” of a fight, unless formalized boxing or wrestling. As far as street fighting goes, anything goes. So if you want to trade insults with me, feel free. If you want to trade compliments with me, feel free. But don’t hurl empty, hypothetical threats at me; fill them up with ultimatums and contingencies. Peace.||||reg||1
